---
import '../styles/home.css';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
const repository = 'https://github.com/Coly010/rtistree';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Rtistree — Programmable graphics for AI agents</title>
    <meta name="description" content="An open-source graphics engine for AI agents. Create reproducible artwork, refine individual parts, and export usable assets with built-in art-direction guidance." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://rtistree.dev/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Rtistree — Programmable graphics for AI agents" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Artistry, rooted in code. A tree of editable layers. Room to keep creating." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://rtistree.dev/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="header wrap">
      <Brand />
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/docs/getting-started/">Docs</a><a href="/examples/">Examples</a><a href={repository}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero wrap">
        <div class="intro">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> OPEN SOURCE · v0.5.1 ALPHA</p> <!-- x-release-please-version -->
          <h1>Artistry.<br /><em>Rooted in code.</em></h1>
          <p class="lede">Programmable graphics for AI agents. Turn an idea into a tree of editable layers, then shape every detail until it feels right.</p>
          <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Make your first image <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/docs/agent-setup/">Connect your agent →</a></div>
          <div class="install"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span><code>npm install rtistree</code><button id="copy-install" aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button></div>
          <p class="install-note"><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/rtistree">View on npm ↗</a> <span>·</span> Node.js 22+ <span>·</span> MIT</p>
        </div>
        <div class="artboard">
          <div class="board-heading"><span>VERDIGRIS WATCH</span><span>ASSET STUDY / 004</span></div>
          <div class="sprite-stage">
            <div class="stage-label">512 × 640 <span>TRANSPARENT PNG</span></div>
            <img class="sentinel" src="/assets/guard.png" width="512" height="640" alt="Procedurally drawn knight in green and steel armour holding a raised sword and shield" />
            <div class="coordinate">x 256<br />y 570</div>
          </div>
          <div class="asset-strip"><img src="/assets/sword.png" width="512" height="640" alt="Matching sword" /><img src="/assets/shield.png" width="512" height="640" alt="Matching shield" /><img src="/assets/coffer.png" width="512" height="640" alt="Wooden coffer" /><div><strong>One source.<br />Many branches.</strong><a href="/examples/">Explore the trial ↗</a></div></div>
          <div class="board-footer"><span class="status-dot"></span> MADE WITH RTISTREE <span>JS → SCENE → PNG</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="capabilities wrap"><span>SCENE GRAPH</span><span>LOCAL EDITS</span><span>SEEDED PROGRAMS</span><span>MCP + CLI + SDK</span><span>REPLAYABLE EXPORTS</span></div>
      <section class="workflow wrap">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">THE WORKFLOW</p><h2>Every image has roots.</h2><p>Rtistree takes its name from artistry, drops the “a”, and puts a tree at its heart. Your artwork keeps its connected layers, its source and its history—so you can keep shaping it.</p></div>
        <ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Construct</h3><p>Compose JSON or YAML scenes, or draw with seeded JavaScript programs. Start with a representative sample.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Inspect & refine</h3><p>Render a crop, check a silhouette, revise a pose. Apply focused edits with history and undo.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Export & replay</h3><p>Export PNG, JPEG, TIFF, PDF, SVG or a portable project. Preserve the source and evidence behind the result.</p></div></li></ol>
      </section>
      <section class="principle wrap"><p class="eyebrow">CRAFT IS PART OF THE PROCESS</p><h2>A valid file is only<br />the beginning.</h2><div><p>A walk can render perfectly and still go backwards. Our asset trial did. That feedback now informs Rtistree’s shipped guidance: check ground contact, connected anatomy and shared perspective before making a whole asset pack.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/agent-art-workflow/">Read the art-direction guide →</a></div></section>
      <section class="closing wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">START SMALL. MAKE SOMETHING.</p><h2>Your first image is a text file away.</h2></div><a class="button primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Open the quickstart ↗</a></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap"><Brand /><p>Built by <a href="https://github.com/Coly010">Colum Ferry</a>. Released under MIT.</p><a href={repository}>Contribute on GitHub ↗</a></footer>
    <script>
      const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('#copy-install');
      button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText('npm install rtistree'); button.textContent = 'Copied'; }
        catch { button.textContent = 'Select command'; }
        setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 2000);
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
